%description:
Tests the AccECN option (RFC 9768 section 3.2.3) with the default
accEcnOptionPolicy="rfc". The first SYN-ACK carries the option with each
field (section 3.2.3.2.1), and so do the ACK of the SYN-ACK and the first data
segment of the client, whose payload becomes smaller by the option. Then the
recommended scheme of section 3.2.3.3 applies: the option goes on an ACK after
a byte count changed, with each field that ever changed, in the order that
needs fewer fields. ECT(0) data gives an AccECN0 option with EE0B alone; after
the CE mark on A004, it has EE0B and ECEB. The data of the server (B005)
carries no option, because no count changed.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 3000"
*.srv_app.sendScript="2.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.tcptester.script="a4 ce"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S E W N 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[0.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S W 500:500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize NOP AccECN0(e0b=1,ceb=0,e1b=1)
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: A W ack 501 win 16384   Option(s): NOP AccECN0(e0b=1,ceb=0,e1b=1)
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N 1:1013(1012) ack 501 win 16384 ECT(0)   Option(s): NOP AccECN0(e0b=1,ceb=0,e1b=1)
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N ack 1013 win 16384   Option(s): NOP NOP NOP AccECN0(e0b=1013)
[1.205 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N 1013:2037(1024) ack 501 win 16384 CE # marking CE
[1.407 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A W N ack 2037 win 16384   Option(s): AccECN0(e0b=1013,ceb=1024)
[1.409 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N 2037:3001(964) ack 501 win 16384 ECT(0) 
[1.611 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A W N ack 3001 win 16384   Option(s): AccECN0(e0b=1977,ceb=1024)
[2.001 B005] A.1000 < B.2000: A W N 501:1501(1000) ack 3001 win 16384 ECT(0) 
[2.203 A006] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N ack 1501 win 16384   Option(s): NOP NOP NOP AccECN0(e0b=1001)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
